ENVIRONMENT AND JENKINS CONFIGURATION
-------------------------------------
- Jenkins is running on an Ubuntu AWS EC2 instance.
- Java 21 is installed / intended for the Jenkins build.
- Jenkins Maven tool installation name: M3
- Jenkins JDK tool installation name: JDK21
- Jenkins SonarQube server configuration name: SonarCloud
- Jenkins SonarQube server URL: https://sonarcloud.io
- Jenkins job name used during setup: java-maven-sonarcloud (job names can vary)
- Pipeline definition: Pipeline script from SCM
- SCM: Git
- Repository URL: https://github.com/Samina-05/sonar-qube-java-project.git
- Branch: choose the branch that contains the latest project files (main or master)
- Script Path: java-maven-sonarcloud-project/Jenkinsfile

WHY THE SCRIPT PATH INCLUDES A FOLDER
-------------------------------------
The Jenkinsfile and pom.xml are not in the root of the GitHub repository.
They are inside java-maven-sonarcloud-project/, so Jenkins Script Path must be:
java-maven-sonarcloud-project/Jenkinsfile

The Maven commands must also run from the folder containing pom.xml:
dir('java-maven-sonarcloud-project') { ... }

WHAT WE DID: STEP BY STEP
-------------------------
1. Created a sample Java Maven project.
   - Calculator.java contains simple calculator methods.
   - CalculatorTest.java contains JUnit 5 tests.
   - pom.xml defines Maven build settings, JUnit, JaCoCo coverage, and Sonar Maven Scanner.
   - Jenkinsfile defines the CI/CD pipeline.

2. Pushed the project to GitHub.
   - Repository: Samina-05/sonar-qube-java-project
   - The project files are inside the java-maven-sonarcloud-project/ subfolder.
   - Both main and master branches exist. This is okay, but Jenkins must use the
     branch that contains the current Jenkinsfile and pom.xml.

3. Created a SonarQube Cloud account/project.
   - Organization key: samina-05
   - Project key: Samina-05_sonar-qube-java-project
   - Automatic Analysis was not selected because the intended analysis is run by Jenkins.

4. Prepared Jenkins on Ubuntu EC2.
   - Opened the Jenkins dashboard.
   - Maven is configured under Manage Jenkins > Tools with the name M3.
   - Java 21 is the intended build JDK.

5. Installed the SonarQube Scanner for Jenkins plugin.
   - This plugin adds the SonarQube server configuration section in Jenkins.

6. Added the SonarCloud token to Jenkins Credentials.
   - Credential kind: Secret text
   - Example credential ID: sonarcloud-token
   - The credential ID is a label; the actual token must remain secret.

7. Configured the SonarQube server in Jenkins.
   - Manage Jenkins > System > SonarQube servers
   - Name: SonarCloud
   - URL: https://sonarcloud.io
   - Authentication token: the saved SonarCloud credential

8. Created a Jenkins Pipeline job.
   - Selected Pipeline script from SCM.
   - Configured Git repository URL and the correct branch.
   - Set Script Path to java-maven-sonarcloud-project/Jenkinsfile.

9. Fixed the Jenkinsfile path error.
   - Initial error: Jenkins could not find the Jenkinsfile.
   - Cause: Jenkinsfile was in a subfolder, not the repository root.
   - Fix: set Script Path to java-maven-sonarcloud-project/Jenkinsfile.

10. Fixed the Maven working-directory error.
    - Initial error: Maven could not find pom.xml in the Jenkins workspace root.
    - Cause: pom.xml is inside java-maven-sonarcloud-project/.
    - Fix: wrap Maven build and Sonar scan commands in:
      dir('java-maven-sonarcloud-project') { ... }
    - Artifact and report paths must include the subfolder prefix.

11. Addressed the Java compiler version error.
    - Errors seen: "release version 17 not supported" and later
      "release version 21 not supported".
    - These errors mean Maven was running with a JDK that could not compile for
      the configured release. The Java used by Maven on the Jenkins agent must
      match the configured JDK.
    - Java 21 home path found on Ubuntu:
      /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-amd64
    - Jenkins Tools JDK name intended: JDK21
    - pom.xml compiler release was changed to 21.
    - Verify this is fixed by checking `mvn -version` in the Jenkins build log;
      it should report Java 21. If it does not, correct Jenkins JDK configuration.

CURRENT PIPELINE STAGES
-----------------------
1. Checkout
   Downloads source code from GitHub using checkout scm.

2. Build and Test
   Runs `mvn clean verify` from java-maven-sonarcloud-project/.
   This compiles the Java application and runs unit tests.

3. SonarCloud Scanning
   Runs the Maven Sonar scanner using:
   - Project key: Samina-05_sonar-qube-java-project
   - Organization: samina-05
   - Host URL: https://sonarcloud.io
   The Jenkins server configuration name used by withSonarQubeEnv is SonarCloud.

4. Quality Gate
   Runs waitForQualityGate and aborts the pipeline if the gate fails.
   This requires a working SonarQube Cloud webhook to Jenkins and an accessible
   Jenkins URL. A webhook URL usually ends with:
   /sonarqube-webhook/
   Do not assume the gate is configured for 80% unless that condition has been
   set in SonarQube Cloud Quality Gate settings.

5. Publish Artifact
   Archives the JAR from:
   java-maven-sonarcloud-project/target/*.jar

POST ACTIONS
------------
- Publishes JUnit test reports from:
  java-maven-sonarcloud-project/target/surefire-reports/*.xml
